    "id": "GNSS_IGS_cum_sta_crd_dsc_1",
    "stac_version": "1.1.0",
    "description": "This derived product set consists of Global Navigation Satellite System Station Coordinate Discontinuities available from Crustal Dynamics Data Information System (CDDIS). The product provides the official, curated history of trajectory breaks and coordinate offsets across the global tracking network of the International GNSS Service (IGS). Generated by the IGS Reference Frame Coordinator at IGN, this cumulative product identifies the precise epochs, solution identifiers, and physical causes of step changes and velocity modifications in multi-year GNSS station coordinate time series.\nDiscontinuities result from documented equipment alterations (such as receiver or antenna replacements), local geophysical events (including co-seismic displacements and post-seismic relaxation from earthquakes), and geodetic monument maintenance. Delivered in compressed Solution INdependent EXchange (SINEX) format, this product is a companion to cumulative IGS reference frame solutions (e.g., IGS20, IGb14), enabling continuous piece-wise linear modeling and coordinate velocity estimation without bias across decades of space-geodetic observations.",
